KZ2 patch 6070: the PSO key's split in a [perf-psokey] line. Diagnostic; no behaviour change.

Written here. [perf-walk]'s "pso: key" (the walker's PSO lookup before the cache probe: 0.8-3 ms a frame in Corinth
Sands) is split in five parts, timed only while RSX_PERF's walk window is on (LDW_T0/LDW_ADD): rs+fpconst
(decode_render_state, rsx_fp_collect_constants, the alpha reference), vp (the VP identity: 2029's memo compare or the
FNV), fp (the FP hash or its memo), units+inputs (the unnormalised-unit loop, the translator inputs, the WPOS and ddy
scans of the FP), tail (ld_pso_key_tail). Printed once a second as
`[perf-psokey] t=Ns rs+fpconst A vp B fp C units+inputs D tail E` (ms in the period). It says which part a PSO key memo
(the walker plan's item 3) would have to remove.
diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index e2ba02c..ce2ea4a 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -2505,6 +2505,10 @@ static DWORD WINAPI rsx_perf_thread(LPVOID unused)
                     d[RSX_PERF_W_D_POST_T] * tk, d[RSX_PERF_W_D_RS_T] * tk,
                     d[RSX_PERF_W_D_BAR_N], d[RSX_PERF_W_D_BAR_T] * tk, d[RSX_PERF_W_D_OMRT_T] * tk, d[RSX_PERF_W_D_SM_HIT_N],
                     d[RSX_PERF_W_D_UNIT_SKIP_N], d[RSX_PERF_W_D_RM_SKIP_N]);
+            if (d[RSX_PERF_W_ON])   /* patch 6070: the split of [perf-walk]'s "pso: key", ms in the last period */
+                fprintf(stderr, "[perf-psokey] t=%.0fs rs+fpconst %.1f vp %.1f fp %.1f units+inputs %.1f tail %.1f\n", tnow,
+                        d[RSX_PERF_W_PK_RS_T] * tk, d[RSX_PERF_W_PK_VP_T] * tk, d[RSX_PERF_W_PK_FP_T] * tk,
+                        d[RSX_PERF_W_PK_XI_T] * tk, d[RSX_PERF_W_PK_TAIL_T] * tk);
             if (d[RSX_PERF_W_ON])   /* patch 2080: NV3089 blits (whole method, its GPU mirror, the guest copy) */
                 fprintf(stderr, "[perf-nv3089] t=%.0fs n=%lld blit %.1fms (gpu %.1fms, copy %.1fms rows %lld)"
                                 " bytes %.2fMB\n", tnow, d[RSX_PERF_W_NV3089_N], d[RSX_PERF_W_NV3089_T] * tk,
